cisions before fabrication.</p></section><section id="options"><p class="eyebrow">MATERIALS &amp; APPROACHES</p><h2>Find the right fit.</h2><div class="options-grid"><div><h3>Brand identification</h3><p>Develop logos, names and feature signs for a particular space.</p></div><div><h3>Information and navigation</h3><p>Organize clear directions, room names or service messages.</p></div><div><h3>Campaign and event graphics</h3><p>Create signs with a defined purpose and display period.</p></div></div></section><section><h2>Where it can work</h2><ul class="check-list"><li><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg>Business openings</li><li><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg>Interior and storefront refreshes</li><li><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg>Events and temporary campaigns</li></ul></section><section class="faqs"><h2>A few useful answers.</h2><details><summary>Can I show a reference photo?<span>+</span></summary><p>Yes. Explain what you like about it, such as finish, scale or composition, so the concept can be adapted to your project.</p></details><details><summary>Do I need to know the material first?<span>+</span></summary><p>No. Describe the use and setting; material options can be evaluated against those requirements.</p></details></section></article><aside class="product-aside"><p clas